.TH SIEFS 8
.SH NAME
siefs \- look inside and change a SieFS image from the host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B build/host/siefs
.I image command
.RI [ argument ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B siefs
runs on the build machine (Linux). It mounts
.IR image ,
does one command, and commits. Paths are inside the image; files it
creates are root's.
.B make
uses it to copy changed files into
.BR build/disk.img .
An encrypted home cannot be read without its password.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR ls " [" \fIpath\fR "], " tree " [" \fIpath\fR ]
A directory: mode, links, owner, group, size, name; or the whole tree
.RB ( / :
directory,
.BR @ :
symbolic link).
.TP
.BI cat " path\fR, " "" stat " path"
A file's contents; its object number, mode, links, owner, size, parent.
.TP
.BI put " hostfile path\fR, " "" get " path hostfile"
Copy a file in (replacing it) or out.
.TP
.BI mkdir " path\fR, " "" rm " path\fR, " "" rmdir " path"
Make a directory, remove a file or an empty directory.
.TP
.BI mv " from to\fR, " "" ln " from to\fR, " "" symlink " target path"
Rename, hard link, symbolic link.
.TP
.BI chmod " mode path\fR, " "" chown " uid" : "gid path"
Permissions (octal) and owner.
.TP
.BI truncate " size path"
A file's new size.
.TP
.BR attr " \fIpath\fR [\fIname\fR [\fIvalue\fR]]"
List a file's attributes, show one, or set one.
.TP
.BI rmattr " path name\fR, " "" find " name value"
Remove an attribute; the objects with this attribute.
.TP
.B df
Blocks, free, freed (usable after the next commits), objects, commit.
.TP
.BR grow " [" \fIsize\fR ]
Take the whole image file (made
.I size
bytes first).
.TP
.BI snap " name"
A snapshot of
.B /
(the USB image's
.BR factory ,
the installer's source).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0; 1 on an error; 2 for an unknown command.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
build/host/siefs build/disk.img ls /
build/host/siefs build/disk.img put notes.txt /tmp/notes.txt
build/host/siefs build/disk.img attr /tmp/notes.txt project SIEOS
.fi
